sam: Heads-up — the chat payload change (conversation.messages -> messages[].content.value) lands Tuesday in staging. We need a compatibility plan for customers on older SDKs.
jess: I lean server-side shim in the gateway to avoid bloating SDKs. Pro: one place to patch everyone. Con: tenant-specific rules and potential perf tax.
lee: Gateway shim makes sense functionally but can add latency for short requests. Do we have microbenchmarks for a JSON transform?
maria: Quick bench: naive rewrite is ~+2–3ms median for 512B payloads, but p99 jumps on large batched payloads. Sample logs attached in staging.
maria: Example of the minimal translator I'm proposing:
```js
// router middleware
if (req.body.conversation && !req.body.messages) {
  req.body.messages = req.body.conversation.messages.map(m => ({
    role: m.role,
    content: { type: 'text', value: m.text }
  }));
}
```
sam: Ops concern: runtime memory churn and CPU at p99 when we see many small requests. If gateway shim is too costly, consider header-driven opt-in with fallback. e.g. `X-Redwood-Compat: rewrite=v1` or `X-RW-Version`.
jess: Another path: ship a lightweight SDK patch that translates client payloads on older versions. Hosted customers get server shim; self-hosted or old SDK users can opt into the SDK patch. Tradeoff: rollout friction vs ongoing operational cost.
lee: Proposed rollout: 1) implement gateway opt-in shim behind a feature flag; 2) release SDK patch that sets the compat header for supported versions; 3) canary enable per-tenant and monitor. Telemetry is critical before widening.
maria: Telemetry fields we should emit: `rewrites.count`, `rewrites.latency_ms.p50/p95/p99`, `rewrites.failures`, `rewrites.per_tenant`, and `request_size_bucket` to correlate with spikes.
sam: Agreed. Ownership: @ops for feature-flag plus kill switch, @devex for SDK patch & release notes, @eng-runtime for benchmarks and perf guardrails.
ops: I can add the feature flag and rollout controls. Will implement a circuit breaker: disable rewrites when rewrite.latency.p99 > 200ms or error rate delta > 1%.
devex_bot: staging canary scheduled Thu 10:30am. Will auto-notify on >2% error uplift and post telemetry summary. :robot_face:
jess: One more: document the compatibility header format we expose to customers: `X-Redwood-Compat: rewrite=v1`. I'll draft an RFC follow-up with migration steps and changelog blurb. :+1:
